00:56:18.550 --> 00:56:41.990
<v Ira Glass>If you'd like to get a cassette of this or any of our programs, call us here at WBEZ in Chicago. Look us up in the book or call 312-948-4680. Or you know you can get tapes from our website, where perhaps in an economically unsound decision, we also make it possible for you to listen to our programs for free at www.thisamericanlife.org.
<v Ira Glass>如果你想获得这期或我们任何节目的录音带，请致电我们在芝加哥的WBEZ。在书中查阅我们或拨打312-948-4680。或者你知道你可以从我们的网站获取磁带，在那里，或许是一个经济上不合理的决定，我们也让你能够免费收听我们的节目：www.thisamericanlife.org。

00:56:41.990 --> 00:56:55.350
<v Ira Glass>There you can also find, this week, a cartoon by Chris Ware, who I interviewed at the beginning of the program today, a cartoon about superheroes and their power over us. It's really just beautiful. Chris, by the way, is the author of Jimmy Corrigan: The Smartest Kid on Earth.
<v Ira Glass>在那里你还可以找到，本周，由克里斯·韦尔（Chris Ware）绘制的一幅卡通画，我在节目开头采访了他，关于超级英雄以及他们对我们的影响的卡通。真的很美。克里斯，顺便说一下，是《吉米·科里根：地球上最聪明的孩子》的作者。

00:56:55.350 --> 00:56:58.160
